<title>ISRAEL: Israel's Supersol Q1 net down.</title>
<headline>Israel's Supersol Q1 net down.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-05-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Super-Sol Ltd.</p>
<p>		     (in thousands of shekels except per share data)</p>
<p>				Q1 97     Q1 96</p>
<p>Revenue		  1,002,492   843,173</p>
<p>Operating profit	  38,730    38,000</p>
<p>Net Profit		  19,860    21,363</p>
<p>EPS			    1.15	1.22</p>
<p>Note: The decline in net profit was mainly due to the acquisition in February of Shekem Ltd's supermarkets for 245 million shekels. Super-Sol also paid 10 million shekels for the Shekem supermarkets' inventory.</p>
<p>Super-Sol reiterated it was studying the possibility of raising about $100 million in a share offering in the United States during 1997.</p>
<p>($1 = 3.39 shekels)</p>
<p>-Tel Aviv newsroomm, 972-3-537-2211 TCC</p>
</text>
